# Copy

Users are not engineers. UI text is product, not debug output.

## Never leak the implementation

- no raw enum / slug / status / identifier values — map through a label constant
- no shell commands, file paths, env var names, or table names
- no stack traces or provider error strings verbatim — summarise, detail behind a collapsed "Technical details" element
- pair a raw id with its human name when the id must show (`Order 1000000`)
- full-page errors: **error-pages** rule (sentence-case H1, no HTTP codes, no red)

Bad: `Job status: pending_worker` · `Restart the queue`
Good: `Ready for review` · `Nothing has run yet`

## States name the fix

- errors say what to do next, not only what broke — one human line + collapsed details
- empty states say what will fill them and offer the action
- disabled controls say why, next to the control
- every list has designed empty, loading, and error copy

## Voice

- second person, active voice, present tense
- Title Case for headings, buttons, labels; sentence case for body and helper text
- numerals for counts (`3 targets`)
- specific button labels naming the action (`Approve output`, not `Continue` / `Submit` / `OK`)
- no `Are you sure?` — state the consequence (`Send this step back for regeneration?`)

## Characters

- `…` not `...`
- curly quotes `’` `“` `”`
- non-breaking space between value and unit or key (`10 MB`, `⌘ K`)
- loading text and placeholders end with `…`
- placeholders show an example, not a restatement of the label
- `Intl.DateTimeFormat` / `Intl.NumberFormat` — never hand-rolled formats
